## Control {{controlId}}: Control the Use of Removable Media on System Components

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization controls removable media usage within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through device configuration policies and endpoint protection rules documented in "Removable Media Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
**Endpoint Removable Media Controls:**
{{deviceConfigurationsCount}} device configuration profiles enforce removable media restrictions:
{{#if configurations}}
{{#each configurations}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{platformType}}){{#if description}} — {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Policies enforce:
- USB mass storage device access restricted or blocked on managed endpoints
- Removable media (USB drives, SD cards, external hard drives) require encryption before CUI transfer
- CD/DVD burning disabled on endpoints processing CUI
- Bluetooth file transfer disabled
{{else}}
Device configuration policies for removable media have not been established.
{{/if}}

{{#if appProtectionsActive}}
**Mobile Removable Media:**
Application protection policies prevent CUI from being saved to unprotected external storage on mobile devices.
{{/if}}

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Quarterly review of removable media policy exceptions; annual audit of USB device access logs
- **Frequency:** Quarterly exception review, annual audit
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Removable Media Policy v1.0, USB Device Access Procedure MP-007

**Review Frequency:** Quarterly by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine device configuration profiles for USB restrictions, Defender for Endpoint device control reports, and removable media exception records.

